<title>MEXICO: Transport chief rules out Banco Mexico job- report.</title>
<headline>Transport chief rules out Banco Mexico job- report.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transport and Communications Minister Carlos Ruiz Sacristan has ruled out being a candidate to replace outgoing Banco de Mexico governor Miguel Mancera, Mexico City newspapers reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a lot of challenges to overcome in the next few years and this is what I am going to dedicate myself to,&quot; he told reporters on Monday.</p>
<p>Ruiz Sacristan had been rumored to be in the running for the governor's job at the central bank, which comes open at the end of the year.</p>
<p>He had once worked as an administrator at Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
